# RayBork M4 Castle sample: a keep, four corner towers, a gatehouse, and a ground plane.
# Every face is counter-clockwise when viewed from outside the part, so the opaque
# back-face culling pass keeps the outward surfaces. The renderer's front face is
# counter-clockwise in the right-handed, Y-up world.
#
# Texture coordinates use 2 m tiles: one 128x128 stone tile covers 2 m of world
# surface, so a 6 m wall maps U 0..3 and a 4.6 m gatehouse wall maps V 0..2.3.
#
# Parts: ground, keep, tower_nw, tower_ne, tower_sw, tower_se, gatehouse.

# Six axis-aligned normals shared by every box face.
vn 0 0 1
vn 0 0 -1
vn 1 0 0
vn -1 0 0
vn 0 1 0
vn 0 -1 0

g ground
v -9 0 -9
v -9 0 9
v 9 0 9
v 9 0 -9
vt 0 0
vt 9 0
vt 9 9
vt 0 9
f 1/1/5 2/2/5 3/3/5 4/4/5

